      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "A warehousing order you enter by hand has no sales or purchase order behind it, so Warehousing gives it its own number. LN fills in the origin, the transaction type and the order type, and you check them. For a transfer inside one company, this one order carries the whole move: first shipping out of the source, then receiving into the destination."
      }
